 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**Possibly, but it’s too early to count on clear air tomorrow, Sunday, October 18.** Singapore’s NEA expects showers and weaker winds that could reduce smoke drifting in from Kalimantan, but haze from Sumatra may still reach Singapore. Its latest published PSI forecast is for *today*, October 17—not Sunday—and remains **Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy**. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nIf you’re planning to be outdoors tomorrow, check NEA’s next-day PSI forecast when it’s issued and the **1-hour PM₂.₅ reading** shortly before you go out. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
